In the continued interest of "doing it wrong", I decided to try
playing a tourist for my second ascension. Never again.
Tera was easily 75+ tries in the making, ranging from the power of
Team Ant, to one annoying run which ended in brain death from a master
mindflayer... on the freaking ascension run. I didn't keep count of
each run, though 3 made it to the PYEC, 2 to the ascension run.

As a large part of the tourist difficulty comes from their lame
earlygame, especially their lack of good equipment, I made a habit of
erasing bones files after a failed attempt(played on 3.4.3 Windows
graphical, not the online server), as it seemed far too cheap to win
based on a previous run's equipment.

We join Tera in the Mazes of Menace, starting with absolutely nothing
special: no blessed items, no random roll tool, no tins of spinach(one
run did end up with two of these, sending my STR right up to 18 before
ever levelling). After a bit of running around darting monsters for a
bit of XP, DL3 saw Tera finding her first good weapon, a trident.
Gleefully dancing around for a bit, Tera resumed her trek, now having
a real melee weapon without having to pop into the mines first(that
happened too much, resulting in several deaths for the sake of a real
melee weapon). Most notable about this run, which didn't happen on any
others, Tera found a dwarf loitering around a shop on DL5, decked with
not only full armor including dwarvish mithril, not only entirely
uncursed armor, but the mithril was +1. Again, first time I'd gotten
either a full set of armor or negative AC before the mines.

Tera wanted to charge down to Sokoban for the hopes of a bag of
holding, as her average STR wasn't cutting it in terms of carrying
capacity. Sadly, Team Ant threatened to intervene on DL8 with three
fire ants camping the upstair, and so Tera was forced to go the mines
route. The mines were vaguely uneventful, the gnomes and dwarves
weren't too much trouble with negative AC, Iczhak's store had all the
candles I needed, the temple was unaligned, and Mine's End was "The
Mimic of the Mines", as wikihack calls it. One luckstone later, Tera
took her leave of the mines, fatally poking a black unicorn on the way
back up for a horn, and taking a brief leave to get unihorn up to
basic proficiency on the early levels of the dungeon.

Now armed with an even better source of poke(though sadly having to
give up her shield for it) and better attack from leveling up, Team
Ant's vanguards fell, allowing a sojurn to Sokoban. The final zoo was
quite hectic, though tactical Elbereth usage and heavy potion chugging
kept the monsters at bay, leaving the grand prize of a bag of holding.
Portable Stash was go. An aligned altar was found on DL11, and
sacrifice farming soon(1500ish turns) resulted in a Blessed Rustproof
+0 Magicbane. Tera, having found her ultimate pokestick, dashed to
upperlevels to get dagger up to basic, then wielded Magicbane for the
rest of the dungeon(barring pickaxe moments).

Tera charged down through the middungeon, finding the portal on DL14.
As she was only level 12 at the time, she proceeded downward for
several more levels, grabbing a bugle from a barracks for the castle
drawbridge, hitting level 13 on monster XP, and quaffing a potion of
gain level for level 14. The quest went rather well, despite needing
an Elbereth fight at the outset, as she was swarmed by spiders and
centaurs without any way to charge into the quest building. The Master
of Thieves went down well, an Identify spellbook were found in the
interim levels, and the PYEC was taken by it's rightful master. Cue
happy dance.

Only the wand of wishing eluded Tera's grasp, and she was quite keen
to get it, as she was still using the armor set from DL5, slightly
upgraded with scrolls, but still only AC -3. A staircase rush for
victory soon brought Tera to Medusa's Lair. This wasn't very good, as
Tera was hoping to find a source of levitation by then, though none
presented itself. A quick dig later brought Tera down to the Castle.
//At this point, I had a few options considered, most of them
involving using the wand of wishing to get a source of levitation if
Perseus wouldn't deliver.

The castle went rather well, barring an annoying master mindflayer(I
had run a genocide on mindflayer earlier, forgetting that uncursed
scrolls wouldn't get the master type as well) who was intent on
summoning monsters with a wand of create monster. Repeated playings of
AEAGF sent the monsters to their squishy doom, and the front room of
the castle was cleared out quickly. Slight scary moment upon meeting a
titan in the lower hallway, but the Random Number God delivered to me
a grey elf... with a wand of death. One dead elf later, one quick zap,
and the titan was gone. More dancing occured upon grabbing the wand of
wishing(0:1).

The first wish went towards blessed +2 silver dragon scale mail,
grabbing reflection and real AC in one swoop. A PYEC invoke went down,
and the wand was back to (1:3). Next grabbed a blessed +2 fixed helm
of brilliance, a blessed horn of plenty, and blessed fixed +2
gauntlets of power(got +0). The wresty wish was saved in case of
emergency getting back out of Medusa. Thankfully, Perseus delivered on
the boots, though their cursed nature was a bit annoying.

Next, Tera made a very nasty blunder by forgetting that wishes
increment the prayer timeout, and 4 of them in a row was a bit much.
Not wanting to waste my precious holy water on getting the boots off,
I charged up to the aligned altar(I say THE, because it was literally
the only aligned one in the game). Several thousand turns were wasted
trying to wait out the prayer timeout(I kept waiting until the 95%
section of the rnz function, but as I didn't know there was 4
additional timeouts added on, that was probably a very low chance
instead). Eventually, Tera shouted a very long string of swear words,
and holywatered the boots, letting her get back to the ground, and
start the sacrifice fun to get the prayer back to normal.

After getting all her stuff together, by rushing through all the shops
and sideareas of the dungeon to collect anything useful, Tera returned
several thousand turns later to the altar, and wrested the final wish
for the Blessed Eye of the Aethiopica(for the MP regen and
branchport). The branchport took her stash to Sokoban, and she
proceeded down into Gehennom.

Gehennom was as usual, with Jubilex easily dispatched with a wand of
digging, Asmodeus falling quickly, Baalzebub likewise, Orcus falling
with 2 charges left in his wand of death, Vlad fell in 4
turns(lolchemy), the Wizard's tower was cleared out without needing a
single Elbereth, and the vibrating square took forever to find.
//After getting horribly fed up with the square, I took a pickaxe to
the level, cutting out circles in the walls every other square's worth
until I found it. I found it on the second circle cut, but still...

Also of note, Orcustown had two rings of excellence, a cursed -2 ring
of increase damage, and an uncursed +1 ring of resistance. Normally
not very interesting, but the PYEC soon bumped them up. The ring of
damage got up to +3 by the end of Gehennom, and against my better
judgement, I charged it again, though the Random Number God was happy
at the time, and gave me a +5 ring. The ring of protection hit +2
after checking my stash one last time, and got a very happy increase
of +3 at the sanctum, getting a +5 bonus there too. After the stash
check, Tera ran through Gehennom with a pickaxe, cutting paths through
the walls to make the ascension run much easier and less maze like.

The Wizard fell to a digging/death combo attack from the diagonal to
kill him without waking him. Now bearing all the ascension artifacts,
Tera rushed to the vibrating square and performed the ritual. The
sanctum featured liches who were far too fond of summon nasties, but
some Elbereth magic, two potions of full healing, and stabbity magic
from Magicbane soon cleared out the area. Then started the wierd part,
and I must ask anyone posting here to try to help me understand WHAT
JUST HAPPENED HERE?!? Upon entering the temple, the high priest was
dead, with the amulet gone. Thinking back to earlier in the Sanctum,
Tera remembered one other odd thing that had happened: Yeenoghu had
been there too. Still, it seemed rather strange, so Tera ran after
Yeno(he'd escaped upstairs). After a fight on the Vibrating Square
floor, sure enough, Yeenoghu had killed the high priest and stolen the
Amulet of Yendor. Tera did not dance as expected at finding the
amulet, as she was still VERY confused at the whole turn of events.

The mysterious force was amazingly mean, causing level 45 to be done
four times, and level 38 done FIVE. Grr...
The MoM run was very clean, though, and Tera soon reached the Plane of
Earth.

Plane of Earth was clean, with few annoying enemies. Took a bit too
long to find the exit, though the PYEC helped again, letting me
recharge the bell of opening to find the portal when the Amulet told
me was was very warm.

Plane of Air was good by usual standards(aka, I didn't DIE). 2 potions
of full healing were needed here, though the portal was found without
needing to kill all the hard monsters.

Plane of Fire was messy, with an archon poking Tera repeatedly in the
face, and monster swarms all around. The portal was found halfway
across the map, though I can't call it being found quickly, as I had
to fight through far too many enemies to get there.

Plane of Water was very clean, with the portal being found by my
Searching intrinsic after about 100 turns.

Astral plane brought me my pet angel(I hadn't found a single ring of
conflict in the game so far, so not really a problem). Tera charged up
the right side to get away from twin archliches in the middle-bottom.
Famine fell easily, then fell easily again, as Tera crowd-surfed
through to the altar. 2 more potions of full healing were demolished,
leaving only 1 FullHeal and 5 ExtraHeal potions. However, these were
not needed, as the altar was neutral, and so Tera rose up into the
ranks of those players foolish enough to try a tourist ascension!
